    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0326" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.77/1574</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-29T19:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 29, 1916, 7 p.m</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Has the American International Corporation communicated to the Department the
                    outcome of <hi rendition="#italic">pourparlers</hi> with Russian interests?
                    Pending receipt of further information I am addressing to the Foreign Office a
                    request that no action possibly prejudicial to American interests be taken
                    without previous consultation with me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
